<https://example.org/dmo/id/contraindication/a1c-test-in-people-of-african-mediterranean-or-southeast-asian-descent-with-hemoglobin-variants> a dmo:Contraindication ;
    rdfs:label "A1C test in people of African, Mediterranean, or Southeast Asian descent with hemoglobin variants" ;
    dmo:contraCode "a1c-test-in-people-of-african-mediterranean-or-southeast-asian-descent-with-hemoglobin-variants" ;
    dmo:rationale "If you’re of African, Mediterranean, or Southeast Asian descent or have family members with sickle cell anemia or a thalassemia NIH external link, an A1C test can be unreliable for diagnosing or monitoring diabetes and prediabetes. People in these groups may have a different type of hemoglobin, known as a hemoglobin variant, which can interfere with some A1C tests." ;
    dmo:severity "Relative" ;
    dmo:triggerCriteria "people of African, Mediterranean, or Southeast Asian descent or have family members with sickle cell anemia or a thalassemia NIH external link" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "If you’re of African, Mediterranean, or Southeast Asian descent or have family members with sickle cell anemia or a thalassemia NIH external link, an A1C test can be unreliable for diagnosing or monitoring diabetes and prediabetes. People in these groups may have a different type of hemoglobin, known as a hemoglobin variant, which can interfere with some A1C tests." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-a1c-test> .

